[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MIL-STD-498 IRS (Interface Requirements Specification) - Military Quad Copter RTOS

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Scope

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1.1 Identification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-001-MILUAV
TITLE: Interface Identification
STATEMENT: This document shall specify interface requirements for the Military Quad Copter RTOS, including ground control station, sensor, actuator, and communication interfaces.
RATIONALE: Clear interface identification ensures proper system integration and interoperability.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1.2 System overview

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-002-MILUAV
TITLE: Interface Overview
STATEMENT: The Military Quad Copter RTOS shall interface with ground control stations, sensor systems, actuator systems, communication networks, and payload systems to enable autonomous military UAV operations.
RATIONALE: Interface overview establishes the context for all interface requirements.

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 2. Referenced documents

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-003-MILUAV
TITLE: Interface Standards
STATEMENT: All interfaces shall comply with MIL-STD-1553B, ARINC 429, CAN bus, Ethernet, USB, and military communication protocols as specified in applicable military standards.
RATIONALE: Standard interface protocols ensure interoperability and maintainability.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. Requirements

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3.1 Ground Control Station Interface

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-004-MILUAV
TITLE: Command and Control Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide a secure command and control interface to ground control stations using encrypted TCP/IP communication over military-grade radio links with automatic frequency hopping.
RATIONALE: Secure command and control interface enables safe and reliable UAV operation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-005-MILUAV
TITLE: Mission Data Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide mission data interface for uploading mission plans, downloading mission results, and real-time mission monitoring with data integrity verification.
RATIONALE: Mission data interface enables mission planning and post-mission analysis.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-006-MILUAV
TITLE: Video Streaming Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide encrypted video streaming interface with H.264/H.265 encoding, adaptive bitrate, and low latency (<100ms) for real-time situational awareness.
RATIONALE: Video streaming interface provides critical visual information for military operations.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3.2 Sensor Interface Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-007-MILUAV
TITLE: GPS/INS Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with GPS/INS sensors using NMEA 0183 protocol for GPS data and custom binary protocol for INS data with automatic calibration and health monitoring.
RATIONALE: GPS/INS interface provides essential navigation and positioning information.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-008-MILUAV
TITLE: LIDAR Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with LIDAR sensors using Ethernet UDP protocol with point cloud data transmission at 10Hz minimum frequency and automatic sensor calibration.
RATIONALE: LIDAR interface enables obstacle detection and 3D mapping capabilities.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-009-MILUAV
TITLE: Camera Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with EO/IR cameras using GigE Vision protocol with automatic exposure control, image stabilization, and multi-camera synchronization.
RATIONALE: Camera interface provides visual and thermal imaging capabilities for military operations.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-010-MILUAV
TITLE: Radar Altimeter Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with radar altimeter using RS-485 protocol with altitude measurement accuracy of ±0.5 meters and update rate of 50Hz.
RATIONALE: Radar altimeter interface provides accurate altitude information for flight control.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-011-MILUAV
TITLE: Environmental Sensor Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with environmental sensors (temperature, humidity, pressure, wind) using I2C protocol with automatic sensor calibration and health monitoring.
RATIONALE: Environmental sensor interface provides atmospheric data for flight optimization.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3.3 Actuator Interface Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-012-MILUAV
TITLE: Motor Controller Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with motor controllers using CAN bus protocol with redundant communication paths, automatic fault detection, and emergency shutdown capabilities.
RATIONALE: Motor controller interface enables precise flight control and propulsion management.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-013-MILUAV
TITLE: Servo Actuator Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with servo actuators using PWM signals with position feedback, automatic calibration, and fault detection for payload control and stabilization.
RATIONALE: Servo actuator interface enables precise control of payloads and stabilization systems.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-014-MILUAV
TITLE: Payload Deployment Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with payload deployment mechanisms using discrete I/O signals with status feedback, safety interlocks, and deployment confirmation.
RATIONALE: Payload deployment interface enables mission-specific equipment deployment.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3.4 Communication Interface Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-015-MILUAV
TITLE: Line-of-Sight Communication
STATEMENT: The system shall provide line-of-sight communication interface using military-grade radio links with frequency hopping, spread spectrum, and anti-jamming capabilities.
RATIONALE: Line-of-sight communication provides primary command and control link.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-016-MILUAV
TITLE: Satellite Communication Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide satellite communication interface as backup communication link with automatic failover and encrypted data transmission.
RATIONALE: Satellite communication provides extended range and backup communication capability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-017-MILUAV
TITLE: Inter-UAV Communication
STATEMENT: The system shall provide inter-UAV communication interface for formation flying and coordinated operations using mesh network protocols with automatic routing.
RATIONALE: Inter-UAV communication enables coordinated military operations.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3.5 Power Management Interface

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-018-MILUAV
TITLE: Battery Management Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with battery management system using I2C protocol with real-time voltage, current, temperature monitoring, and automatic low-battery protection.
RATIONALE: Battery management interface ensures safe and efficient power utilization.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-019-MILUAV
TITLE: Power Distribution Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with power distribution system using discrete I/O signals for power switching, current monitoring, and fault detection with automatic load shedding.
RATIONALE: Power distribution interface enables efficient power management and fault protection.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3.6 Security Interface Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-020-MILUAV
TITLE: Cryptographic Module Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with FIPS 140-2 Level 3 cryptographic modules for encryption/decryption operations with secure key management and tamper detection.
RATIONALE: Cryptographic module interface ensures secure communication and data protection.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-021-MILUAV
TITLE: Authentication Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide authentication interface for multi-factor authentication including biometric, smart card, and token-based authentication methods.
RATIONALE: Authentication interface ensures secure access control and system protection.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3.7 Data Storage Interface

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-022-MILUAV
TITLE: Mission Data Storage Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with mission data storage using encrypted flash memory with automatic backup, data integrity checking, and secure data erasure capabilities.
RATIONALE: Mission data storage interface ensures data security and operational accountability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-023-MILUAV
TITLE: Flight Log Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide flight log interface for recording system events, sensor data, and operational parameters with automatic log rotation and secure storage.
RATIONALE: Flight log interface enables post-mission analysis and system diagnostics.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3.8 Maintenance Interface

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-024-MILUAV
TITLE: Maintenance Port Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide maintenance port interface using USB 3.0 with secure authentication, diagnostic capabilities, and firmware update functionality.
RATIONALE: Maintenance port interface enables system maintenance and software updates.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-025-MILUAV
TITLE: Diagnostic Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide diagnostic interface for system health monitoring, fault diagnosis, and performance analysis with real-time status reporting.
RATIONALE: Diagnostic interface enables proactive maintenance and system optimization.

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Qualification provisions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-026-MILUAV
TITLE: Interface Testing
STATEMENT: All interfaces shall undergo comprehensive testing including protocol compliance, performance testing, interoperability testing, and security testing with documented test results.
RATIONALE: Interface testing ensures reliable system integration and operation.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Requirements traceability

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-027-MILUAV
TITLE: Interface Traceability
STATEMENT: All interface requirements shall be traceable to system requirements, design specifications, and test procedures with bidirectional traceability maintained throughout development.
RATIONALE: Interface traceability ensures complete verification and validation of interface capabilities.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. Notes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-028-MILUAV
TITLE: Interface Documentation
STATEMENT: All interface specifications shall be documented with detailed protocol descriptions, timing diagrams, signal specifications, and compliance requirements for military applications.
RATIONALE: Interface documentation ensures proper system integration and maintenance.

[[/SECTION]]

